--- !u!114 &-6589275856826560828
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: 'The materials in HDRP can optionally use an RGBA <b>Mask Map</b> to define different texture properties, such as metalness (R), ambient occlusion (G), detail mask (B), and smoothness (A).


      1. In the <i>Hierarchy,</i> expand the <b>Props</b> > <b>Room3</b> > <b>Ball_PF</b> GameObject.


      2. Select the <b>Ball</b> GameObject.


      3. In its <i>Inspector,</i> expand the <i>Brass_Mat</i> Material.


      4. Remove the <b>Mask Map</b> or set it to None, and see that the ball becomes uniformly smooth as the smoothness variations from the Mask Map texture are removed.


      5. Experiment with the <b>Metalness</b> and <b>Smoothness</b> sliders, to change the behavior of the surface.


      6. Undo your changes.'
