--- !u!114 &-2580129023021358725
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "The High Definition Render Pipeline (HDRP) can simulate the refraction of the light inside materials.\r\n\r\n1. In the <i>Hierarchy,</i> expand <b>Props</b> > <b>Room 3</b> > <b>RoundTable_01</b> > <b>RoundTable_01_LOD0.</b>\r\n\r\n2. Select the <b>RoundTable_GLass_01_LOD00</b> GameObject.\r\n\r\n3. In the <i>Inspector,</i> expand the <i>Glass Dark_Mat Material.</i>\r\n\r\n4. In the <b>Transparency Inputs</b> section, set the <b>Refraction Model</b> to None to disable the refraction entirely. \r\n\r\n5. Undo your change and experiment with the <b>Index Of Refraction</b> slider.\n\r\nRefraction also allows us to create a frosted glass effect, which you can adjust by tuning the <b>Smoothness</b> of the material.\r"
